<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>快速反馈 on Yousa Driven Development | YDD</title><link>https://yousali.com/tags/%E5%BF%AB%E9%80%9F%E5%8F%8D%E9%A6%88/</link><description>Recent content in 快速反馈 on Yousa Driven Development | YDD</description><generator>Hugo -- 0.148.1</generator><language>zh</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:10:25 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://yousali.com/tags/%E5%BF%AB%E9%80%9F%E5%8F%8D%E9%A6%88/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>一周到货两次，Zara 怎样用卖过的数字决定下一批</title><link>https://yousali.com/stories/zara-small-batch-testing/</link><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://yousali.com/stories/zara-small-batch-testing/</guid><description>2005 年起，Caro 等研究者与 Zara 合作改进门店配货流程，依托全球门店每周两次收货的节奏，改用门店库存与销售预测来分配同款不同尺码的补货数量。经实地对照试点，研究估算这套尺码分配流程带来了约 3% 到 4% 的销售增长。</description></item></channel></rss>